I am sitting in the back of the taxi.
It is very cold in Berlin, but the taxi is warm.
The taxi driver is friendly.
"Good evening," he says.
"Where would you like to go?"
I tell him the address.
He nods and starts driving.
We drive through the dark city.
"Are you new in Berlin?" the driver asks.
"Yes, I am new here," I answer.
"Where do you come from?"
"I come from Mexico."
"Mexico is beautiful," he says.
"What are you doing in Germany?"
"I am a software engineer," I explain.
"I work here now."
"That is interesting," he says.
"My name is Maya Flores," I say.
"Welcome to Berlin, Ms Flores," he answers politely.
